ToricInvariants -- Given a projective toric variety, the package computes the degree and codimension of the dual, the Euclidean distance degree, polar degrees, and Chern-Mather class
**************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

Given a projective toric variety X_A defined by a full rank integer matrix A
with the vector (1,1,...,1) in its row space, the package computes the degree
and codimension of the dual (i.e. the A-discriminant variety), the Euclidean
distance degree of X_A, the polar degrees of X_A, and the Chern-Mather class of
X_A. Note that we do not require that X_A is normal. This package uses the
algorithms described in [1] and [2]. For definitions of the objects computed by
the package see [1,2].

References: \break [1] Martin Helmer and Bernd Sturmfels. "Nearest points on
toric varieties." Mathematica Scandinavica 122, no. 2 (2018): 213-238. Arxiv
version: https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.06544.\break [2] Martin Helmer and Bernt
Ivar Utstol Nodland. "Polar degrees and closest points in codimension two."
Journal of Algebra and Its Applications (2017): 1950095. Arxiv version:
https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.02381.

