cmClass -- Computes the Chern-Mather class of a projective toric variety
************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        cmClass(A)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a full rank integer matrix
        with the vector (1,1,...,1) in its row space defining a projective
        toric variety X_A
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * ForceAmat (missing documentation) => a *note Boolean value:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, if A defines a codimension
        two toric variety a faster method will be used by default, setting this
        to true forces the general purpose method
      * Output (missing documentation) => a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,,
        default value RingElement, this can be set to HashTable to return a
        HashTable with all computed values
      * TextOutput (missing documentation) => ..., default value "Quiet", 
  * Outputs:
      * cm, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the Chern-Mather
        class of the projective toric variety X_A pushedforward to the Chow
        ring of the ambient projective space.

Description
===========

This function computes the Chern-Mather class of the projective toric variety
X_A pushedforward to the Chow ring of the ambient projective space, we do not
assume that X_A is normal.

